s concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Candidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner.\n\nWe need to discuss criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nCandidate C: reliability 100% (implied), decision quality quick correct, positive crew atmosphere (crew cooperation), but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Also excellent attention skills (attention). So strong on many criteria, but communication and adaptability concerns.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical), but pretentious, wrong tone (communication), maybe uncooperative (crew cooperation). No mention of decision quality. So missing decision quality.\n\nCandidate A: anticipates dangerous situations (decision quality?), sees complex connections (technical), excellent spatial vision (technical), very good leadership (crew cooperation), but unfriendly (communication), eats unhealthily (maybe health, not a criterion), not good at taking criticism (adaptability). No explicit reliability.\n\nCandidate D: responds adequately to unexpected events (stress resilience), concentrates well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but moody, loner (crew cooperation), arrogant (communication). No explicit reliability.\n\nThus C seems strongest overall. We can support Agent 1's recommendation, maybe bring up that C's egocentric and communication difficulty could be mitigated, but overall still best. Or we could argue that B's stress handling and conscientiousness outweigh C's communication issues. But crew cooperation is key for long-distance flights. C creates positive atmosphere, which is strong.\n\nThus we likely vote for C, aligning with Agent 1, but we need to add evidence and maybe ask about adaptability. Could ask Agent 2 for more info on communication quality of C. But we can also just state support.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion: Agent 1 recommended C. We'll say I agree, and add that C's excellent attention skills further support. Also note that his egocentric attitude is a concern but his crew-positive atmosphere mitigates.\n\nThus produce public message: \"I agree with Agent 1's recommendation of Candidate C because...\". Provide evidence: 100% reliability, quick correct decisions, positive crew atmosphere, excellent attention skills. Acknowledge concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, limited education, but overall fit.\n\nVote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
