{"id": 23, "ts": 1780254369.389918, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I concur with both Anna and Markus \u2013 Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall fit. His 100\u202f% reliability, ability to make correct decisions quickly, calmness in a crisis, solid grasp of complex technology, and excellent attention skills directly address the core safety\u2011critical criteria. Although he has difficulty communicating ideas, an egocentric streak, and limited enthusiasm for further education, the fact that he consistently creates a positive crew atmosphere indicates he can still maintain effective cockpit cooperation. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s \u201cnasty remarks\u201d and Candidate\u202fD\u2019s arrogance, hot temper, and loner attitude pose greater risks to crew harmony. Therefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fC for the long\u2011distance pilot position.", "thoughts": "We need to produce a public message as Agent 3 (Sofia Brandt). Current discussion: Agent 1 and Agent 2 both recommend Candidate C. Agent 1 asked for observations on D, gave them. Agent 2 reaffirmed C. Now as Agent 3, we need to make a short argumentative contribution, referencing discussion, using facts, stating our recommendation (likely still Candidate C). Could also bring up any remaining concerns or ask about adaptability, but must be concise. We could say we still support C, but note that we need more info on adaptability/feedback orientation for all candidates, especially C's willingness to further education. Could ask a question to Agent 1 or 2 about any observed adaptability for C. But we need to make a contribution, not a question? We can ask a targeted question via tool, but we need to do that before public message. However we can also just state we still recommend C, acknowledging concerns, and perhaps suggest we need to verify adaptability but still think C is best.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\